ENTRY            32688   20140401   20140604   20140515       3163
SUBENT        32688001   20140401   20140604   20140515       3163
BIB                 10         36
TITLE      Associated gamma radiation in interaction of 14.9 MeV
           neutrons with natural silicon
AUTHOR     (Hong-Yu Zhou, Fu-Guo Deng, Wei Cheng, Feng-Shou Zhang,
           Qiang Zhao, Jun Su, Li-Ming Dong, Qing Zhu,
           Guo-Ying Fan)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRBNU)
           (3CPRCPR) School of Nuclear Science and Engineering,
           North China Electric Power University, Beijing, China.
REFERENCE  (J,NIM/A,648,(1),192,2011) Main reference
           #doi:10.1016/j.nima.2011.04.014
           (J,PR/C,82,047602,2010)
           #doi:10.1103/PhysRevC.82.047602
FACILITY   (CCW,3CPRBNU)A pulsed Cockcroft-Walton accelerator.
METHOD     (GSPEC,TOF) The sample was placed at a distance
           13.4cm in front of the neutron target. A total gamma-
           radiation measurement(TGRM) technique used in
            (n,xgamma) experiments. The TOF technique is employed
           to reduce the background caused by the primary and
           scattering neutrons.
SAMPLE     The sample is a cylindrical crystal silicon 3.0*3.0
           cm in diameter and weighting 50.52 g.
INC-SOURCE (D-T)The repetition frequency of the pulsed deuteron
           beam is 3.2 MHz. Neutrons incident on the sample are
           produced from the T(d,n)4He reaction. The neutron
           energy in the 0 degree direction with respect to the
           deuteron beam is 14.9 +- 0.5MeV, and the average
           intensity is 5*10E8 n/s in 4pi sr.
DETECTOR   (GELI,SIBAR) Absolute gamma-ray yields are measured
           by a coaxial Ge(Li) detector. The counts of the
           associated particles of 4He are measured by an Au-Si
           detector.
           (SCIN) A plastic scintillator (NE-211) was used as
           the neutron monitor.
HISTORY    (20110607C)Compiled by Xi Tao (CNDC)
           (20140401A) VS. Units MeV->keV corrected in subents:
                       014,015,018,019,021,022,023,024,025.
ENDBIB              36
COMMON               2          3
EN         EN-ERR
MEV        MEV
       14.9        0.5
ENDCOMMON            3
